s the graph of $y=x-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=x-6.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=(0)-6=-6,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=(1)-6=-5,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=(2)-6=-4,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=(3)-6=-3.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $-3$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/99/99188f2a0f8de0054a6375a88a11242bea7e4799cc17552cd9ba0dd00d5a0788.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=x-6.$\n\n![](images/44/44b8f095ef9aca54e6215b1b61c9fad562dd54b0f00b7e9b8e2efdd904dd83e6.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["645e1d5a-90c9-50c4-b1ae-f7aff3a3dba1"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "09af78ca-b5c2-58ed-aee4-4ddfc7a7f013" :answer/id #uuid "09af78ca-b5c2-58ed-aee4-4ddfc7a7f013" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f3/f3b91b84281ef5b4936438c7e92935cbaf15d17ee50b33a27a7bed638391ef74.png" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "29968d51-b8a6-5bee-82fc-d738be24cc8b" :answer/id #uuid "29968d51-b8a6-5bee-82fc-d738be24cc8b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b9/b9758c660c06a62ba10ca7ced102655a3a8f376d31d9c4ef73ec9ea8b33e769b.png" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "06fa8c2f-5b1f-5063-8e88-0b913061880c" :answer/id #uuid "06fa8c2f-5b1f-5063-8e88-0b913061880c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/30/30ea4f86a1a588cd617779bc001935f50b7fa358ecca86efeaf26bde27642627.png" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7083980a-a87f-5d35-b45a-36f6cd7e349b" :answer/id #uuid "7083980a-a87f-5d35-b45a-36f6cd7e349b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/07/07b33747d01621cb73ae464999a8d6a135f0dc579f9e50b250f34b3df9ca4783.png" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f90d513b-aef2-5217-be5f-bd7b7f1eafff" :answer/id #uuid "f90d513b-aef2-5217-be5f-bd7b7f1eafff" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/05/05d10ee3d2e6bc295a7d2e6b07ca726c9c11c159d74f1d81c71fce761fa4275e.png" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ad570f02-ebbc-528a-ba9a-40d1735ee18e" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad570f02-ebbc-528a-ba9a-40d1735ee18e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["09af78ca-b5c2-58ed-aee4-4ddfc7a7f013" "29968d51-b8a6-5bee-82fc-d738be24cc8b" "06fa8c2f-5b1f-5063-8e88-0b913061880c" "7083980a-a87f-5d35-b45a-36f6cd7e349b" "f90d513b-aef2-5217-be5f-bd7b7f1eafff"] :answer-field/correct "f90d513b-aef2-5217-be5f-bd7b7f1eafff" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "5a903cf9-42ce-5563-9b36-303a8f1c1320" :question/id #uuid "5a903cf9-42ce-5563-9b36-303a8f1c1320" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=-x-3.$.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-x-3.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=-(0)-3=-3,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-(1)-3=-4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=-(2)-3=-5,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-(3)-3=-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-4$ | $-5$ | $-6$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/c9/c96b7da7b073986de68a557df8a9dbde16d39566c87eb0b5ba6ac62bd40da7c4.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-x-3.$\n\n![](images/05/05d10ee3d2e6bc295a7d2e6b07ca726c9c11c159d74f1d81c71fce761fa4275e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["ad570f02-ebbc-528a-ba9a-40d1735ee18e"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "e100f2db-5cdc-57b9-ba8