$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=2x-6.$\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=2(0)-6=-6,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=2(1)-6=-4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=2(2)-6=-2,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=2(3)-6=0.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nPlotting these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane: \n\n![](images/95/958c5a848a09e43832324b8afb000348c7630cd2c42e99a51215d48d9895a00e.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of  $y=2x-6.$\n\n![](images/3e/3efb14f33400cd4a6353b93e5d99a826083cca6859785d5bd5d837fb00ad302f.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["39f305ae-b441-5bc6-833a-ae8108df72ec"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "9ae4d764-bdf7-5b4d-982a-b379ea720263" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186054694.py"} [:db/add 17592186054694 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186054694 :knowledge-point/questions ["67365bc6-453f-5a19-82a4-9817c6e05a99" "5a903cf9-42ce-5563-9b36-303a8f1c1320" "5da1545d-7bf4-538f-94f3-464d21187a82"]} [:db/ensure 17592186054694 :knowledge-point/validate]]
